course: dictionary
lesson: 5527
title: Words for places and things in church
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words name one special thing. When you meet one, the rest of the sentence often tells you what it is for. «The building helps too: the font for baptism, the pulpit for preaching, the lectern for reading» lists several church things, and each one has its own job.
explain: A lectern is a tall stand with a sloping top. A speaker puts notes or a book on it and reads while standing up. «Step up to the lectern» tells you it is the place you go to when you speak or read to people.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The font, a big stone bowl for water often near the door, is used for baptism, the pulpit for preaching and the lectern for Bible readings.» Put "a tall stand for a book" in place of lectern and the sentence still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
fact: A lectern is a tall stand with a sloping top.
fact: In church, a lectern holds the big Bible, and a reader reads the Bible passages from it.
fact: In school, a lectern may stand on the stage in the hall for assemblies and speeches.
fact: Some lecterns are shaped like an eagle.
fact: In the same sentence, «font» is a big stone bowl for water, and «pulpit» is used for preaching.
exercise: In church, what is a lectern used for? | Holding water for baptism | *Holding the big Bible for readings | Sitting on during a sermon | Holding flowers for the altar
exercise: «Step up to the lectern.» What is a lectern? | *A tall stand with a sloping top for notes or a book | A kind of window with stained glass | A low bench where people kneel | A large stone bowl for water
exercise: The phrase «eagle lectern» means a lectern shaped like what? | A tree | A boat | A dog | *An eagle
test: In «the font for baptism, the pulpit for preaching and the lectern for reading», which word names the stand used for reading? | Font | *Lectern | Baptism | Pulpit
test: Ella says a lectern is a big stone bowl near the door. Is she right? | No, a lectern is a tall stand with a sloping top | Yes, it holds water for baptism | Yes, it is where people kneel to pray | *No, that is a font, not a lectern
exam: «The speaker walked up to the ___ and read her notes aloud.» | Stained glass | Pew | Font | *Lectern
